 <!-- CARROT:AUTO:END CustomSteerDeltaDown -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:BEGIN CustomSteerDeltaDown -->
-<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="" -->
+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="7b2680b5b1f5ab961afaafa6ef2c4f2fe80b3e07c7171fdd448f5af27df33c88" reviewed-at="2026-11-04T00:00:00Z" -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Higher values reduce steering torque faster; lower values release it more slowly. Zero uses the vehicle’s default release rate.
+
+On Porter II EV, a protective release rate takes priority when opposing driver torque puts the previous command outside Panda’s driver-torque envelope. Maximum steering torque and normal tracking settings are retained.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Existing saved values are not changed automatically. Restart after updating the software.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+This yields steering authority to the driver faster; it does not increase steering strength or automatic-turn capability.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END CustomSteerDeltaDown -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:SETTING:END CustomSteerDeltaDown -->
